{"File":"C:\\Users\\toufi\\Desktop\\firstrun\\README.md","LineNumber":306,"LineContent":"The business plan sets the agent's spending limit. `firstrun econ` reads 64 neatlogs traces and writes [business/drivers.csv](business/drivers.csv) for cfo.ai. The mean run costs $0.0167, and the p95 run costs $0.0508. A 70% margin floor turns those costs into a cap per tier, and `firstrun run --tier scale` stops any run that spends past the cap."}
{"File":"C:\\Users\\toufi\\Desktop\\firstrun\\README.md","LineNumber":314,"LineContent":"The old fixed cap of $0.50 let one bad month cost a Scale customer's fee five times over. The plan, the Scale fix and every assumption are in [business/BUSINESS_PLAN.md](business/BUSINESS_PLAN.md). The cfo.ai model is public at [https://cfo.ai/s/_u5lbrHIl9KX_JQE](https://cfo.ai/s/_u5lbrHIl9KX_JQE). Under the old cap, cash goes negative in month 14."}
